cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If NeoMoM contributes to your research, publication, article,
  presentation, or antenna design, please cite this project and
  acknowledge the original author.
type: software
title: NeoMoM Antenna Modeling Suite
abstract: >-
  NeoMoM is a modern, open-source wire Method of Moments (MoM) antenna
  modeling suite for amateur radio operators. The computational engine is
  written in Fortran and uses Rao-Wilton-Glisson (RWG) rooftop basis
  functions. The suite includes graphical tools for antenna geometry input,
  far-field pattern visualization with geographic map overlay, impedance and
  SWR analysis, and current distribution viewing. NeoMoM is designed to
  provide accurate results comparable to NEC5 while offering a modern,
  accessible workflow for new users.
